6.753\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JPJSK7EV1S0T9HQ\",\"t\":\"Lithos\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/enhanced-weathering-agriculture/1.2\",\"t\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.2\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/enhanced-weathering-agriculture/1.1\",\"t\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JPJSK7EV1S0T9HQ/prj_1JY1YXDBS1S01Y05/pjd_1KS892FHQ1S01TY7/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 30 Jul 2025\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KW33J4MV1S0MC79?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JPJSK7EV1S0T9HQ/prj_1JY1YXDBS1S01Y05/pjd_1M0B3YZQ31S0Z7KK/validation_and_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JPJSK7EV1S0T9HQ/prj_1JY1YXDBS1S01Y05/pjd_1M0B3YC001S0QXW9/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JPJSK7EV1S0T9HQ/prj_1JY1YXDBS1S01Y05/pjd_1KWMQX2H91S0VZZ0/validation_and_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JPJSK7EV1S0T9HQ/prj_1JY1YXDBS1S01Y05/pjd_1KWMQV3QB1S0MP7P/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JPJSK7EV1S0T9HQ/prj_1JY1YXDBS1S01Y05/pjd_1KS8AZFEC1S062DC/validation_and_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nEW\\n1,000Y+\\nUS Southeast Enhanced Weathering Project\\nLithos\\nISSUED\\n12,332.95\\nBUFFER POOL\\n246.661\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Oct 2023 to 01 Jan 2028\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nThis project outlines Lithos Carbon's ERW efforts in the subtropical Southeast U.S., applying superfine byproduct basalt dust to farmland for durable carbon removal. Through rigorous field sampling and a robust analytical monitoring pipeline, Lithos ensures high-integrity CDR quantifications. By sourcing byproduct superfine rockdust directly from nearby quarries and working directly with both smallholders and large farms, Lithos minimizes life-cycle emissions while improving soil health, enhancing cropland productivity, and delivering direct financial benefits to farming communities- enabling the scalable deployment of ERW across hundreds of thousands of acres.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nZFYD\\nApproval date\\n22 May 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nEnhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.2\\nBaseline protocol version\\nEnhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nUS Southeast Enhanced Weathering Project\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nEnhanced Weathering (EW) accelerates the Earth's natural chemical weathering process to remove carbon dioxide from the atmosphere. In chemical weathering, carbon dioxide dissolved in rainwater reacts with minerals in rocks, partly dissolving them and producing stable bicarbonate ions. These bicarbonate ions are transported by rivers to the ocean, where they are safely stored for thousands of years. EW is typically carried out by spreading crushed reactive rocks or minerals on croplands.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n30 Jul 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 4,148.88 tCO₂e removed from US Southeast Enhanced Weathering Project on 25 Mar 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n4,148.879 tCO₂e\\nSequestrations\\n4,617.631 tCO₂e\\n-\\nActivities\\n468.752 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nLithos Southeast\\tMineral & rock\\t26 May 2026\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n18 Aug 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n18 Aug 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n03 Jul 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n03 Jul 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n22 May 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 8\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n12,332.95\\nRetired\\n1,397.302\\nBuffer pool\\n246.661\\nCrediting period\\n01 Oct 2023 to 01 Jan 2028\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n18 Aug 2026\\t6,043.77\\t120.876\\t5,922.894\\n03 Jul 2026\\t4,686.38\\t93.728\\t4,592.652\\n22 May 2026\\t1,524.48\\t30.49\\t1,493.99\\n22 May 2026\\t78.32\\t1.567\\t76.753\\nShowing 4 of 4\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Lithos's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 246.661 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 246.661 certificates.\\n\\nLithos has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"